+Same columns as mtah.load.load_tagging. Both kinds are made to share the real tags'
+imperfections, so validation does not reward leaning on tags harder than the real ones allow.
+
+Phase tags are matched to what the real match's tags look like (measured without labels,
+against our own predictions): "reliable" build-up/progression tags cover ~44% of live play,
+agree with the possessing team ~88% of the time, last ~19 s and start only loosely near a
+possession change (+1.6 s, IQR -2.6..4.2 s); "other" attacking phases cover ~66%, agree ~64%,
+last ~24 s and start -2.4 s (IQR -9.5..1.9 s). They span several possessions, so they are
+context, not switch markers.
+
+Set-piece tags:
   - windows open ~3.5 s before the restart (measured on the challenge kick-offs), with jitter;
   - throw-ins carry no team, as in the challenge export;
   - a share of non-kick-off set pieces is dropped (the real tags are automatic, with misses).
